WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.910
There's still money there. Why won't it let me keep waiting?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.468
You need initial margin to open a position.

00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:15.130
While it's open, you must also meet the maintenance margin requirement.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.740
What you put in at the start isn't how much buffer you'll always have.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.679
Say the initial margin is 100 and the position is down 20.

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:41.458
Ignoring everything else, the equity is now 80.

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:45.360
If the price keeps moving against you, the buffer keeps shrinking.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.532
When equity gets close to the platform's maintenance level,

00:01:10.532 --> 00:01:13.981
the risk system may step in. It doesn't have to wait for zero.

00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:17.430
It depends on the account type, margin mode and product rules.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.760
So if I keep adding money, I'm safe?

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.356
Adding money doesn't change the price direction,

00:01:41.356 --> 00:01:43.701
and it doesn't guarantee you won't be liquidated.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.710
It can pull more money into the same risk.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:00.900
No. One is about opening the position. The other is about keeping it open.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.460
Check equity first, then how far it is from the warning line.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:17.370
Put 100 in a box. Is the other 900 safe forever? Next: isolated margin.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.900
Understand first, then act.
